Chapter: RangeRefineElseLeak

 Refinement must not leak across arms: in the ELSE arm of `i < 200`
 the then fact does not hold - there i is 200..i64-max under the
 outer `i >= 0` guard - so storing i into a 0..255 field is unproven
 and CDX2051 rejects it. A leak of the then arm's 0..199 fact into
 the else arm would let this compile silently; the proven twin lives
 in range-refine-if.

Section: Definitions

  Entry = record {
   code : Integer between 0 and 255
  }

  leak-code : Integer -> Integer
  leak-code (i) =
   if i >= 0
   then if i < 200 then 0 else (Entry { code = i }).code
   else 0

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text (leak-code 45))
  end
